  "pick": {
   "x": 1280,
   "y": 1060,
   "w": 560,
   "size": "m",
   "fill": "pink",
   "text": "My pick: A, Last Call.\n\nIt is the only one that still reads as a face at chip size. Its hand-picked colour ramps also carry over cleanly: BOLT-7 and Old Dax came out of the same method and sit together as a set.\n\nB has the best pose and mood, but it leans on a prop and the face goes muddy below 64 px.\n\nC has the best light, but the faces turn soft and mask-like, and the dithered haze shimmers in motion. Its lighting could work for big story moments, such as a reveal or the finale."
  },
